  "organizations": {
    "eyebrow": "Factions & Orders",
    "heading": "Organizations",
    "items": [
      {
        "name": "FBMM",
        "fullName": "Federal Bureau Of Magic Management",
        "type": "Federal Intelligency",
        "icon": "star",
        "accent": "tertiary",
        "sigil": "",
        "motto": "Responsibility And Integrity",
        "founded": "1934",
        "headquarters": "New Heaven City",
        "jurisdiction": "Federal Level",
        "purpose": "The goal of the FBMM is to monitor and control the use of magic. Its purpose is to prevent users from misusing their magical abilities or using magic for personal or harmful purposes.\n\nThe FBMM protects ordinary people from the misuse of magic and other supernatural abilities. It regulates the use of magic, investigates magical incidents, and arrests individuals who abuse or illegally use their powers.\n\nIts jurisdiction covers the NUS (New United States), where it operates as the federal agency responsible for regulating and controlling the use of magic.",
        "description": "The history of the FBMM began in 1934, during the first major period of widespread magical use. Magic was increasingly being used by ordinary people for useful and beneficial purposes. However, this period also saw a growing number of individuals misusing magic for harmful and criminal purposes.\n\nOne major event would change everything.\n\nA separatist group known as **The Chosen** carried out a terrorist attack at **Hotel Proper 9**, located in the NUS capital of **New Heaven City**. The attack proved catastrophic for the police at the time. Numerous people were killed or injured, and although the perpetrators were eventually subdued, the consequences of the attack were devastating.\n\nThe incident exposed how unprepared the existing law-enforcement agencies were when dealing with large-scale magical threats. It became clear that conventional police forces were not equipped to properly respond to individuals who could use powerful magic for terrorism and other criminal purposes.\n\nIn response, the government established the **Federal Bureau of Magic Management (FBMM)**.\n\nThe FBMM was originally proposed to the President by two Elven founders. Its primary mission was to identify and eliminate magical threats before they could develop into major incidents. In its early years, the agency was staffed primarily by Elves and Half-Elves, who possessed greater knowledge and experience with magic.\n\nOver time, the FBMM became increasingly diverse, with Humans and other races joining its ranks. Today, the FBMM serves as the NUS's primary federal agency for regulating and protecting the nation from the misuse of magic.\n\nIts responsibilities have expanded beyond simply responding to magical threats. The agency now regulates the use of magic, investigates supernatural incidents, protects the general population, and enforces laws concerning magical abilities throughout the NUS.",
